{title: 318 - Whiter Than Snow}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #318 • WHITER THAN SNOW • 12.11.13.11}
{lyricist: James Nicholson}
{composer: William G. Fischer}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 318}
{meta: tune WHITER THAN SNOW}
{meta: meter 12.11.13.11}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Lord Jesus, I [F#dim]long [G]to be perfectly [F#dim]whole;
[G]I want Thee [F#dim]forever [G]to [F#dim]live [Bm/F#]in [F#dim]my [G]soul;
[G]Break [Bm]down [G]every idol, [C/G]cast out [G]every foe;
[G]Now wash me, and [F#dim]I [Em]shall [F#dim]be [G]whiter [F#dim]than snow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F#dim]Whiter [G]than snow, yes, whiter [C/G]than [G]snow;
[G]Now [C/G]wash [G]me, [C/G]and [G]I shall be [F#dim]whiter than [G]snow.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Lord Jesus, [F#dim]look [G]down from Thy [F#dim]throne [Bm/F#]in [F#dim]the [G]skies,
[G]And help me [F#dim]to [G]make a complete [Bm/F#]sacrifice;
[G]I [Bm]give [G]up myself, and [C/G]whatever [G]I know;
[G]Now wash me, and [F#dim]I [Em]shall [F#dim]be [G]whiter [F#dim]than snow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Lord Jesus, [F#dim]for [G]this I most [F#dim]humbly entreat;
[G]I wait, blessed [F#dim]Lord, [G]at Thy [F#dim]crucified feet,
[G]By [Bm]faith, [G]for my cleansing; [C/G]I see [G]Thy blood flow;
[G]Now wash me, and [F#dim]I [Em]shall [F#dim]be [G]whiter [F#dim]than snow.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Lord Jesus, [F#dim]Thou [G]seest I patiently [F#dim]wait;
[G]Come now, and [F#dim]within [G]me a [F#dim]new [Bm/F#]heart [F#dim]create;
[G]To those who [C/G]have sought [G]Thee,
[G]Thou never [C/G]said'st [G]No;
[G]Now wash me, and [F#dim]I [Em]shall [F#dim]be [G]whiter [F#dim]than snow.
{end_of_verse}
